      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T21:42:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we initialize rd_stats_y and rd_stats_uv here?",
      "parentUuid": "cce3c9ca_459d0d80",
      "revId": "99c08b9f89de7dc6b97f33c96242b7f3bd33255f",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "869f0380_f1b6bc58",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/rdopt.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 6319,
      "author": {
        "id": 5020
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T21:52:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Should we initialize rd_stats_y and rd_stats_uv here?\n\nThere is additional cost to that which may accumulate if this function is called frequently. If they\u0027re not used then leaving them uninitialized with the added documentation is all right. There might be better ways to structure this code, but I haven\u0027t looked at.",
      "parentUuid": "6cf05d1e_c6f4c3ef",
      "revId": "99c08b9f89de7dc6b97f33c96242b7f3bd33255f",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "50b39dc5_67e9831f",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/rdopt.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 6319,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-20T21:55:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. This code was added a long time ago (2018, I think). So these two variables have always been uninitialized. I believe they are meant to be output-only parameters.\n\nIf we initialize these two variables to silence valgrind, I suggest we initialize them to invalid values (with `av1_invalid_rd_stats`). This will catch incorrect use of these two variables before they are properly initialized.",
      "parentUuid": "6cf05d1e_c6f4c3ef",
      "revId": "99c08b9f89de7dc6b97f33c96242b7f3bd33255f",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
